 ],
 "note": "Measured on the TouringCarTimes side-on photo of Wilson's Belmont (right side, mirrored to our side; the model was traced from the same frame, so positions carry over 1:1): Bristol Street box with red bar and SUNDERLAND No.1 on the rear quarter, Vauxhall/Mobil sticker on the rear door, ESSO board on the front door, Champion on the front wing, name on the rear door window. Checked on Getty LAT 2201201054 (Silverstone round 13, right side): same layout, Dunlop on both bumpers, no Valvoline sticker, so the Valvoline logo on the rear door in the TouringCarTimes photo (another round) is left out. Wheels: gold 5-spoke with polished lip from Getty 2201201054 (on track; the TouringCarTimes photo shows gold dish-type wheels, so the wheels changed during the year). Only right-side photos exist: the left side is assumed to mirror it."
